{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.JonesNormalisation","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.BigOperators","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Pi"],"declarations":31,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.jonesFn_wordBraid_eq_tlStateSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.jonesFn_wordBraid_eq_tlStateSum","kind":"theorem","line":359,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L359-L368","doc":"**Framing-corrected trace in Temperley–Lieb state-sum form.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.braidTrace_wordBraid_eq_leadProd_add_tlStates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.braidTrace_wordBraid_eq_leadProd_add_tlStates","kind":"theorem","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L339-L357","doc":"**Leading scalar product + Temperley–Lieb loop corrections.**\nWhen the site weight is normalised (`(∑ k, w k) * wi = 1`), the `s ≡ false` state contributes\nthe naive per-crossing scalar product `(ℓs.map (letterLeadScalar q qi)).prod`, and the\nremaining states `s ≠ (fun _ => false)` collect all Temperley–Lieb cup-cap contractions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.tlStateMatrix_const_false","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.tlStateMatrix_const_false","kind":"theorem","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L329-L337","doc":"At the all-`false` (identity-smoothing) state, the Temperley–Lieb word operator is `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.tlStateWeight_const_false","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.tlStateWeight_const_false","kind":"theorem","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L322-L327","doc":"At the all-`false` (identity-smoothing) state, the state weight is the naive per-crossing\nscalar product `∏_{ℓ ∈ ℓs} letterLeadScalar q qi ℓ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.braidTrace_wordBraid_eq_tlStateSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.braidTrace_wordBraid_eq_tlStateSum","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L307-L320","doc":"**Mass identity on `B_{m+1}`, Temperley–Lieb state-sum form (Option 3).**\nThe normalised Markov trace of `wordBraid ℓs` equals the state sum of the factorised scalar\nweights `tlStateWeight q qi ℓs s` times the normalised quantum traces of the Temperley–Lieb\nword matrices `tlStateMatrix q qi ℓs s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.hol_eq_tlStateSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.hol_eq_tlStateSum","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L289-L305","doc":"**Bridge between Option 1 and Option 3 (algebra level).**\nThe non-abelian multiplicative integral `hol q qi ℓs` of a braid word expands as the\nTemperley–Lieb state sum over `s : Fin ℓs.length → Bool`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.tlStepFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.tlStepFactor","kind":"def","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L283-L287","doc":"Single-crossing state summand: `c(ℓ) • 1` for `b = false`, `-e_a` for `b = true`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.tlStateMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.tlStateMatrix","kind":"def","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L277-L281","doc":"The Temperley–Lieb word operator of a state `s` on `ℓs`: the ordered product of `tlProjector`\nat crossings with `s i = true` (and `1` at crossings with `s i = false`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.tlStateWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.tlStateWeight","kind":"def","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L271-L275","doc":"The scalar weight of a Temperley–Lieb state `s` on a braid word `ℓs`: the product of\n`letterLeadScalar q qi ℓ` at identity-smoothed crossings (`s i = false`) and `-1` at\ncup-cap-smoothed crossings (`s i = true`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.stateProd_smul_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.stateProd_smul_eq","kind":"theorem","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L261-L269","doc":"Scalar factors pull out of `stateProd` in any `R`-algebra `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.stateProd_const_false","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.stateProd_const_false","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L253-L259","doc":"Evaluating `stateProd` at the all-`false` state recovers the ordered product of the\n`false`-channel factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.prod_map_add_eq_sum_stateProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.prod_map_add_eq_sum_stateProd","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L235-L251","doc":"**Non-commutative binary state-sum expansion.**\nIn any semiring `A`, the ordered product of binary sums `∏ (f a false + f a true)` along a\nword `w` equals the sum over all states `s : Fin w.length → Bool` of `stateProd f w s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.sum_fin_succ_bool","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.sum_fin_succ_bool","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L228-L233","doc":"Splitting a finite sum over `Fin (n + 1) → Bool` by the head bit `b : Bool`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.stateProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.stateProd","kind":"def","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L221-L226","doc":"Ordered product along a word `w : List α` in a binary state `s : Fin w.length → Bool`,\nchoosing `f a false` or `f a true` at each position. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.transport_eq_lead_sub_tlProjector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.transport_eq_lead_sub_tlProjector","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L209-L219","doc":"**Universal two-channel decomposition of a crossing transport.**\nBoth positive and negative crossings satisfy `T(a, ε) = c(ε) • 1 − e_a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.letterLeadScalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.letterLeadScalar","kind":"def","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L204-L207","doc":"The identity-channel scalar of a signed crossing letter: `q` for a positive crossing,\n`qi` (`= q⁻¹`) for a negative crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.tlProjector_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.tlProjector_sq","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L189-L202","doc":"**The Temperley–Lieb loop relation over a general `CommRing R`.**\n`e_a² = (q + q⁻¹) e_a`, proved from `isHeckeGenerator_braidAt` and `q * qi = 1` alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.tlProjector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.tlProjector","kind":"def","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L184-L187","doc":"The Temperley–Lieb generator `e_a = q • 1 − Ř_a` at strand `a` on `V^{⊗(m+1)}`, defined\nover an arbitrary `CommRing R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.jonesFn_wordBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.jonesFn_wordBraid","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L161-L169","doc":"**The framing-corrected trace** of a word's braid is the same functional of its\nmultiplicative integral, times the strand and writhe factors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.braidWritheZ_wordBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.braidWritheZ_wordBraid","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L148-L159","doc":"The writhe of the braid a word spells is the word's signed letter count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.signedLength","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.signedLength","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L143-L146","doc":"The signed letter count of a word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.braidTrace_wordBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.braidTrace_wordBraid","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L134-L141","doc":"**Mass identity, Markov form.** The normalised Markov trace of the braid a word spells\nis the site-weighted trace of the word's multiplicative integral:\n`tr_M(β_ℓ) = wi^{m+1} · Tr(K^{⊗(m+1)} · Hol(ℓ))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.heckeActionN_wordBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.heckeActionN_wordBraid","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L120-L132","doc":"The representation of a word's braid is the multiplicative integral of the word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.heckeActionN_letter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.heckeActionN_letter","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L102-L118","doc":"A letter's braid, represented in the Hecke algebra and then on `V^{⊗(m+1)}`, is its\ntransport. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.hol_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.hol_append","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L96-L100","doc":"**Non-abelian multiplicative-integral composition law (Option 1).**\nThe holonomy of a concatenated braid word is the ordered product of the two holonomies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.hol_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.hol_cons","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L93-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.hol_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.hol_nil","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L91-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.hol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.hol","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L87-L89","doc":"The discrete multiplicative integral of a word: the ordered product of its transports. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.transport","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.transport","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L82-L85","doc":"The R-matrix transport of a letter: `Ř_a` for a positive crossing,\n`Ř_a − (q − q⁻¹) = Ř_a⁻¹` for a negative one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.wordBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.wordBraid","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L78-L80","doc":"The braid a word spells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.letterBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Torsion.MassTraceMarkov.letterBraid","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Torsion/MassTraceMarkov.lean#L74-L76","doc":"The braid generator of a letter, with the sign of the crossing. ","signatureChunk":0}]}